# Harness project

This repo is a file agent: an OpenAI-compatible chat loop, tools confined to one workspace, and a JSONL trace in that workspace's `session.log`.

- `src/harnh3x/config.py` holds `PROVIDER`, `API_KEY`, `API_URL`, `MAX_TOKENS`, `CONTEXT_LIMIT`, `MODEL`, `MAX_TURNS`, `COMPACT_AT`, `MAX_TOOL_RESULT`, the fetch/search/feed limits, `SHELL_TIMEOUT`, `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT`, and `SHELL_MAX_OUTPUT`, the file listing and search caps, `PDF_MAX_PAGES`, `PREVIEW_ROWS`, `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`, `WIKIPEDIA_LANG`, and `BASE_DIR` (default `~/.harnh3x`, expanded when it is absolute or starts with `~`). Sessions live in `BASE_DIR/workspaces`. `MEMORY_FILE` is `BASE_DIR/memory.md`, shared across sessions. `~/.config/harnh3x/harnh3x.yaml` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/harnh3x/harnh3x.yaml`) is YAML and can set the API key, API URL, and those tunables except `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, and `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`. A non-empty process environment variable overrides the file for those scalars, and a working-directory `.env` fills variables that are not already set. `HARNH3X_CONFIG` selects another file; an empty value skips it. `mcp` is a mapping of stdio servers (`command`, `args`, `env`, `timeout`, `description`, `instructions`, `include`, `exclude`). Environment variables do not override `mcp`. If `harnh3x.conf` exists and `harnh3x.yaml` does not, startup exits and names both files. `MCP_SERVERS` holds the validated servers. `provider` is `openai` (default) or `anthropic`. Startup exits when `api_key` is unset, and when `api_url` is unset for `openai`. For `anthropic`, the key is `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` when that variable is set, otherwise `api_key`; `OPENAI_API_KEY` does not override it. `api_url` defaults to `https://api.anthropic.com`. `max_tokens` defaults to 8192. `context_limit` is optional and applies to both providers; when it is unset, Claude compaction uses 200000 and the OpenAI path asks Ollama's `/api/show`. `--yolo` stays a launch flag.
- `src/harnh3x/failures.py` holds the fixed answers a turn returns when it cannot finish (timeout, unreachable API, rejection prefix, max turns, empty answer) and `is_failure_answer`; the OpenAI and Anthropic paths both use those strings.
- `src/harnh3x/anthropic_api.py` translates the stored transcript to the Anthropic Messages API and maps the stream back into the same assistant message. `get_client()` returns that client when `provider` is `anthropic`.
- `src/harnh3x/prompt.py` builds the system prompt: date and OS, a one-line workspace listing, the saved memory keys, the prompt contract, and the skill menu. It accepts `now` for tests, `yolo` to add the unsandboxed-session sentence, `project` to name a granted folder and point code changes there, `rules` for that folder's Cursor rules, and `coding` to replace the assistant contract with a coding-agent prompt.
- `src/harnh3x/rules.py` reads `<project>/.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc` only in a coding session. `alwaysApply` rules go in the system prompt. `globs` may be a comma-separated line or a YAML list; a matching file tool appends that rule once. A symlink that resolves outside the project is skipped. A bad frontmatter block is skipped.
- `src/harnh3x/tools/` defines the tool schema and the sandbox. Each skill module exports its schemas and functions. `TOOLS` is the full domain catalog assembled from those modules. `tools/scope.py` adds the session's sandbox, yolo, and project sentence to each sent schema.
- `src/harnh3x/skills/` holds `SkillRegistry` plus one `SKILL.md` per skill: `file-ops`, `shell`, `python`, `coding`, `research`, `reference`, `http`, `documents`, `data`, `memory`, `tasks`, and `hardware-diagnosis`. A skill may live in a category subdirectory (`skills/<category>/<name>/SKILL.md`, any depth). Each `SKILL.md` starts with YAML frontmatter: `name` matches the folder and `description` is the menu line; `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, and `allowed-tools` are optional. `allowed-tools` is a space-separated list of tool names and is the skill's tool list; skills may share a tool. `description` says what the skill does and when to load it, since the menu is all the model sees before loading; the body has no "When to Use" section. The body is freeform Markdown with workflow and reporting conventions, and is returned by `load_skill`. The loop sends `load_skill`, `unload_skill`, and schemas for loaded skills only, each tool name once; several skills can be loaded at once. Configured MCP servers are extra skills in category `mcp`. `SkillRegistry` starts each one and runs `initialize` and `tools/list` when it is built, and keeps that process for `load_skill`. Their tool schemas come from the server, not from `TOOLS`, and are sent only once the skill is loaded. `src/harnh3x/mcp/` is the stdio client. The menu line is the config `description`, else the server's `serverInfo.description`, else the first line of its `instructions` that is not a heading, else the server name and version, the tool count, and the first five tool names. A server whose tools collide with a built-in tool is dropped with a warning. Its `load_skill` result is the config `description`, the config `instructions`, the server's `initialize` instructions, and its resource list. The child is not Seatbelt-sandboxed. `unload_skill` drops its schemas and leaves the process up. `reset()`, `resume()`, and process exit close it. An MCP skill is omitted when an `http` or `https` URL in its `env` is not accepting connections. A handshake that cannot finish removes that skill from the menu.
- `src/harnh3x/agent/` owns `Session` and `run`. `Session.reset()` starts a new conversation in a new workspace, keeping the model, `yolo`, `project`, `coding`, and `debug`. `Session.resume()` reloads a workspace's `transcript.json`, restores `project` and `coding` from that file, replays skill loads, and refreshes the system prompt. `reset()` and `resume()` clear the set of glob rules already appended. A transcript with no `project` clears any launch grant. A transcript with no `coding`, or with `coding` false, clears a launch coding session. A non-boolean `coding` value fails resume. `coding` is stored in the transcript when the session is a coding session. `yolo` and `debug` stay launch flags and are not stored in the transcript. `reset()` and `resume()` keep `debug`.
- `src/harnh3x/cli.py` is the CLI, exposed as the `harnh3x` console script. `--project PATH` grants sandboxed read, write, and shell access to one existing directory that must not overlap the session workspace; `/` is rejected. Relative paths and the shell working directory use that folder. `--coding` requires `--project` and starts a coding session: a coding system prompt, and Cursor rules from that project. The flag is stored in `transcript.json` and restored by `/resume`. Ctrl+N keeps it. Plain output and the header print `Coding` on the line after `Project:`. `--debug` shows the system prompt once at the start of the session, and again only when that prompt changes, plus the other messages sent on each completion, in cyan panels that keep the last three lines until a click expands them. It is not stored. Ctrl+N and `/resume` keep it. Plain output prints `Debug` on the line after `Coding`. The status bar shows `Debug`. `--answer-only` hides those panels. The summary call is not shown. `--yolo` disables the seatbelt sandbox: read tools may open any path, shell and Python may run any program, including sudo, and `run_shell` is `/bin/sh -c`, so pipes, redirects, chaining, and `$` run. HTTP tools may use any host, including localhost and private addresses. File mutation tools stay in the workspace, or in the project when one is granted. A tty session uses Textual (`src/harnh3x/tui/`: `text.py` wrapping and panel text, `transcript.py` the turn and compaction model, `export.py` answer export and clipboard, `panels.py` the transcript widgets, where `Thinking`, `DebugBox`, and `ToolBox` share `CollapsiblePanel`, `pickers.py` the numbered list screens, where the model, resume, and export screens share `NumberedPicker`, `modals.py` the overlays, `app.py` the app and runners; `__init__` re-exports every public name): a header whose title is Harnh3x, then the workspace, the project when one is set, and Coding when the session is a coding session, then the transcript. A status bar above the composer shows the model, context used against the model's limit (with the percentage when the limit is known; that segment turns yellow at 80% of the `COMPACT_AT` point and red at or past it), and how many built-in skills and tools are available, then how many MCP servers are accepting connections and how many tools they offer; the MCP counts are omitted when there are none. The package version sits at the far right of that bar. It also shows `YOLO` in bright yellow when the sandbox is off, `Debug` when `--debug` is set, and a red warning when a configured MCP server is unavailable, ending with `Ctrl+W for warning details`. Ctrl+W, or a click on the status bar, opens the reason. Those marks stay after Ctrl+N and `/resume`. The bar is hidden when it has nothing to show. Plain stdout still prints `YOLO — sandbox off` before the workspace and model. `--answer-only` stays the final answer only. The composer takes Enter to submit, and Shift+Enter or Ctrl+J for a newline; it grows with its text up to eight rows. Up on its first row and Down on its last row walk the past prompts of this transcript and this run, keeping the draft. Typing `/` shows the matching commands above the composer, and Tab completes the first one. While a turn or `/compact` runs, a line above the composer shows a spinner, the phase (waiting, thinking, writing, running a named tool, compacting, stopping), the elapsed time, and `Esc to stop`. Esc sets `session.abort`, kills tool child processes, and when the worker returns clears the abort, adds a `Stopped.` note, and re-enables the composer; the app stays open. Ctrl+Q and `/exit` quit and stop the running request. Ctrl+N and `/new` start a new session in a new workspace and refresh the header path. Ctrl+H and `/details` hide or show every thinking box, tool box, debug box, and compaction note, including ones added while they are hidden. In Terminal.app (`TERM_PROGRAM` is `Apple_Terminal`), `translate_legacy_key` in `text.py` turns Backspace carrying `\x08` into Ctrl+H and a Ctrl+W with no character (Option+Backspace with Meta on) into Alt+Backspace before bindings run; other terminals pass keys through unchanged. User messages carry an accent bar; an answer that `is_failure_answer` accepts carries a red bar; notes are dim and command errors are red. Copy and export results show as toasts. `src/harnh3x/commands.py` is the one slash-command table: `COMMANDS` names each command, whether it takes an argument, and its usage line; `help_lines()` builds the Commands block of both help texts; `dispatch()` routes a parsed command to the caller's handler and reports unknown names and wrong argument shapes. The plain prompt and the composer both use it; `parse_command` in `harnh3x.agent` splits the typed text. `/help` opens a scrollable box of commands and hotkeys that Escape closes. The pickers are bordered modal boxes. `/resume` opens a list of past sessions and restores that transcript; typed text that is not a number filters that list. `/compact` forces a context compaction. `/export PATH` writes one answer, or every answer, to a markdown file. More than one answer asks which response, or all of them. The file is the answer text only. Icons at the bottom right of a response copy it or write it to a markdown file; the path box starts with `answer-YYYYMMDD-HHMM.md` and names the directory a relative path uses. The path may be outside the workspace; a relative path uses the project directory when one is granted, otherwise the working directory. Each model round's tool calls share a bordered box, in the order the API produced them. A call appears when it starts, as `name  key=value`, marked `…` until `session.on_tool_done` reports its result, then `✓`, or `✗` with the first line of an `Error` result; replayed calls have no mark. That box keeps the last three lines, with each value cut at 80 characters, until a click expands it to every line and the full values; a box with a cut value can expand even when it fits in three lines. A click on any collapsible box leaves focus in the composer; a focused box toggles with Enter or Space. Thinking and the answer update while the completion streams; each thinking box keeps the last three lines until a click expands it. While output is arriving, the transcript stays at the bottom until the user scrolls up, and scrolling back to the bottom follows again. A context compaction shows Compacting context… while the summary runs, then a Context compacted note, and the agent answer is rendered as Markdown. One-shot on a tty starts that view before the request so tokens are visible as they arrive, and waits for Enter to close when the turn included reasoning. Plain stdout writes reasoning and the answer as the tokens arrive. `/resume` reprints a finished transcript in that same order, with the collapsed thinking panel for a finished reasoning block. Piped input and `--answer-only` stay plain stdout. `--model` with no name uses the Textual list on a tty and a numbered prompt otherwise. Tests live under `tests/`, one `test_*.py` per subsystem (`test_agent_loop`, `test_session`, `test_compaction`, `test_skills`, `test_cli`, `test_tui_helpers`, `test_tui_app`, `test_file_ops`, `test_shell`, `test_project`, `test_research`, `test_http`, `test_documents_data`, `test_memory_tasks_prompt`, `test_config`, `test_anthropic`, `test_mcp`, `test_system_info`, `test_tools_core`); fakes used by more than one file are in `tests/helpers.py`.
- Export new public symbols from `src/harnh3x/__init__.py` `__all__`.

Poetry with `package-mode = true` and a `poetry-core` build backend so pip and pipx install the `harnh3x` script. Pytest uses `pythonpath = ["src"]`. Format with Ruff. Do not commit `src/.env`.

A new tool, or a looser path or shell check, needs a matching test.

```python
# BAD: a second model constant next to the loop
MODEL = "other"

# GOOD: change the constant in src/harnh3x/config.py
from harnh3x.config import MODEL
```
